body:
CI was failing because `cell-renderers.test.tsx` used hardcoded UTC timestamps (e.g. `'2026-02-24T08:00:00Z'`) as "today/yesterday/tomorrow" anchors. As calendar time advanced, these became stale and produced off-by-one day assertions.

## Changes

- **`formatRelativeDate` tests** — Replaced all hardcoded ISO strings with `Date` objects computed dynamically from `new Date()` ± N days, making the assertions permanently date-agnostic:

  ```ts
  // Before (breaks as time passes)
  expect(formatRelativeDate('2026-02-25T08:00:00Z')).toBe('Tomorrow');

  // After (always correct)
  const tomorrow = new Date();
  tomorrow.setDate(tomorrow.getDate() + 1);
  expect(formatRelativeDate(tomorrow)).toBe('Tomorrow');
  ```

- **`DateCellRenderer` tests** — The existing mock used `vi.spyOn(Date, 'now')`, which does **not** affect `new Date()` — the call site inside `formatRelativeDate`. Replaced with `vi.useFakeTimers()` + `vi.setSystemTime()` so the system clock is fully frozen at `2026-02-24T12:00:00Z`, making the hardcoded value assertions against that fixture reliable:

  ```ts
  // Before: mock had no effect on new Date() inside formatRelativeDate
  nowSpy = vi.spyOn(Date, 'now').mockReturnValue(...);

  // After: freezes the entire clock including new Date()
  vi.useFakeTimers();
  vi.setSystemTime(new Date('2026-02-24T12:00:00Z'));
  ```

